{"additions":4835,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTE1MTA=","is_bot":false,"login":"williammartin","name":"William Martin"},"baseRefName":"williammartin-multiaccount-draft-07-explain","changedFiles":21,"closedAt":null,"deletions":1,"headRefName":"williammartin-multiaccount-draft-08-evaluation","isDraft":true,"latestReviews":[{"id":"","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nOffline fixtures still access the operator’s native keyring, while other active findings identify broken standard acceptance runs, lost API gateway routing, and missing direct capability-output coverage.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>4 open issues</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Enforce keyring isolation for offline fixtures](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14927#discussion_r4460644833) · New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Keep full acceptance runs usable without ghdebug](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14927#discussion_r4460644885) · New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Preserve the API gateway in isolated lifecycle config](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14927#discussion_r4460644943) · New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Test capability output for keyring isolation](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14927#discussion_r4460645011) · New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nThis final layer of the multi-account prototype stack adds guided setup and evaluation tools around the existing identity system. It remains a draft experiment, not a merge-ready design.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds approval-focused onboarding guidance and evaluation scenarios.\n- Introduces live walkthroughs, offline regression journeys, and reset/downgrade checks.\n- Adds debug-only keyring isolation and a protected acceptance lifecycle.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `script/​multiaccount-review/​08-reset.sh` | Replays reset and stable-binary recovery. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​runner_test.go` | Tests runner setup, interaction, isolation, and cleanup. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​runner_helper_test.go` | Supplies fake gh and SSH executables. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​run.sh` | Adds guided live identity journeys and resource cleanup. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​reset_downgrade_test.go` | Checks configuration preservation across reset and downgrade. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​README.md` | Documents setup, evaluation, limitations, and recovery. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​offline_test.go` | Adds offline identity and routing regression journeys. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​fixture_test.go` | Provides synthetic accounts and simulated Git transports. |\r\n| `script/​identity-e2e/​bootstrap.sh` | Implements account selection, isolated setup, and guided prompts. |\r\n| `pkg/​cmd/​version/​version.go` | Reports when debug keyring isolation is enabled. |\r\n| `internal/​keyring/​keyring.go` | Blocks keyring operations under debug isolation. |\r\n| `internal/​keyring/​isolation_test.go` | Checks isolation preserves existing keyring credentials. |\r\n| `internal/​debug/​config.go` | Adds the debug keyring-isolation setting. |\r\n| `internal/​debug/​config_test.go` | Clears the new setting during test setup. |\r\n| `internal/​config/​identity_isolation_test.go` | Checks isolated login/logout preserves operator tokens. |\r\n| `acceptance/​testdata/​identity/​identity-lifecycle.txtar` | Exercises identity lifecycle and worktree behavior. |\r\n| `acceptance/​README.md` | Documents lifecycle isolation and credential requirements. |\r\n| `acceptance/​acceptance_test.go` | Adds isolation gating and private token-file helpers. |\r\n| `.github/​skills/​setting-up-identites/​tests/​scenarios.json` | Defines offline onboarding and approval-boundary cases. |\r\n| `.github/​skills/​setting-up-identites/​SKILL.md` | Adds guided prototype setup and scoped undo instructions. |\r\n| `.github/​skills/​setting-up-identites/​references/​workflow.md` | Provides inspection, setup, verification, and cleanup examples. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Revie